# Call-site ledger of nodeenv at cb7fc97ebff9792d1fa603fe66baa6fcd5912659.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in nodeenv.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md. nodeenv
# 1.12.0 supports CPython 3.10 and later (setup.py python_requires, no
# upper bound) on Linux, macOS and Windows (its CI) and on Cygwin, MSYS2,
# Solaris/illumos and FreeBSD (README.rst, CHANGES): both sides of every
# is_WIN and is_CYGWIN test run (J4).
# Values used below (nodeenv.md, "Values"):
#   logger: the logging.Logger "nodeenv" of create_logger (line 424), level
#     INFO, with one StreamHandler on sys.stderr. create_logger replaces
#     logging.StreamHandler.emit with its local emit (line 407), so every
#     info, warning, error and critical call of the package has emit as a
#     callee (callback of logging); so has a debug call, since a client
#     can lower the level through logging's documented configuration (J1;
#     ruling of the lead, 2026-11-24).
#   urlopen: nodeenv.urlopen returns what urllib.request.urlopen returns:
#     an http.client.HTTPResponse, or a urllib.response.addinfourl for a
#     file:// mirror (documented) and for ftp (J3).
#   args: the argparse.Namespace of parse_args (make_parser's options).
#   join and abspath: os.path.join and os.path.abspath (lines 44-45).

